      "writtenOn": "2019-04-05T18:07:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Typically EAGAIN means the system call did *not* perform the requested action, because a resource involved was temporarily unavailable.\n\nLooking through this code I think this use is safe because the return values here never come from a system call, but this still feels a bit fragile.\n\nIf a system call return value were introduced in this path, and it returned EAGAIN, that would get mistakenly interpreted by wait_for_ack() caller as meaning damaged ACK i.e. success.\n\nWhat do you think of changing wait_for_ack() return value to an enum, making it clear that the values are not errno values?",
      "revId": "19acfa03c1f3c037abb7210bea83ce9e1dbea1e1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
